  "notes": [
   "No cover email was supplied; the reply is a photographed rate card plus an ISO certificate.",
   "All 30 RFx lines are priced one-to-one in the same order and by the same size as the RFx. Row alignment was checked against sizes and the price sequence, but the photo is skewed, so confidence is capped at about 0.85.",
   "Lines 17–19 (7-ply) and 26–27 (sheet, pad) are priced per kg. The RFx unit for 17–19 is piece; the buyer's system must convert using the stated weights (2.45 kg for line 17, 1.95 kg for line 19; none for line 18).",
   "The rate card does not state flute type or BF, so flute/BF deviations cannot be assessed (e.g. C flute for lines 4 and 6; E flute for mailers). The rate card gives only ply and paper GSM, which match the RFx.",
   "Payment 30 days is shorter than the requested 60 days from GRN. This is a commercial deviation.",
   "Rates are valid till 31 Dec 2026, which is under the 90 days required from the RFx date (22 Sep 2026) and ends before the contract period starts on 1 Apr 2027.",
   "Freight is included for 'Pune district deliveries'. Chakan lies in Pune district, so this is taken to cover it. Incoterm (DAP) is not stated explicitly.",
   "GST rate is not stated, only 'ex-GST' and the GSTIN.",
   "Q2 (FSC), Q8, Q9 (in-house flexo; 1C and 2C printed items are priced but no explicit claim), Q10 and Q11 are not addressed.",
   "The ISO certificate covers the Nashik plant and is valid through the contract period."
  ],
